Fix the two limitations the E2E test reported, plus a third found underneath

The full-pipeline test passed 10/10 but closed by naming two things it had not
proved. Both were real defects.

The fraud detector had latched itself off permanently. WORKFLOW_DETECT_AND_ACT
sized its backpressure queue as every OPEN HIGH/MEDIUM alert ever raised, with
no time bound, and that count only grows. At 106 open alerts against a limit of
100, every run returned throttled=true and added nothing, so no detection rule
would ever execute again. The test read this as backpressure working correctly,
which is exactly how it hides. The queue is now a 7-day rolling window; the same
106 alerts are 47 inside it, and the workflow returns throttled=false with 8 new
alerts where it previously returned zero on every invocation.

The AI FinOps page understated real spend because PROCESS_BL_DOCUMENTS made two
Cortex calls per document and logged neither. Both now write to AI_CALL_LOG with
measured latency, and COMPLETE carries real token counts via COUNT_TOKENS.
PARSE_DOCUMENT is billed per page, so its token columns stay NULL rather than
carrying a guess. Verified live on one document: exactly two rows.

Adding that logging exposed a third defect. AI_CALL_LOG.CALL_ID was
autoincrement start 1 noorder while seeded data already used ids to 703, leaving
69 duplicate CALL_IDs and 66 duplicate LOG_IDs - the same unenforced-primary-key
trap as FRAUD_ALERT.ALERT_ID. It also showed why burning the counter forward is
not a fix: noorder allocates from non-monotonic cached ranges, and consecutive
single-row inserts were measured receiving id 313 then 651. Both columns now
default to dedicated sequences, which repairs the eleven other procedures that
insert without naming CALL_ID without editing any of them. HASH_AGG over every
non-id column is identical to the pre-fix clone.

Also fixed the Extracted Documents table, which stopped at 20 rows while the
metric above it counted the whole table, so 25 documents displayed as "25" and
then listed 20 and the newest five were invisible.

Demo baseline restored after every verification: 423 log rows, 496 alerts,
15 documents, 15 stage PDFs, 10,017 bills, empty compliance queue.